[83.524932, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mcd /tmp/opencode/src/stp && grep -n -A4 -B2 \"Dependencies\\|libgmp\\|Boost\\|cmake\" docs/building.rst | head -100; echo \"---minisat files---\"; dpkg -L minisat | head -50; echo \"---cms files---\"; dpkg -L libcryptominisat5-dev | head -40\r\n6-build against, and the configuration variables worth knowing.\r\n7-\r\n8:STP is built with `CMake <https://cmake.org/>`__, version 3.18 or newer.\r\n9-CMake is a meta build system that generates build files for other tools\r\n10-such as make(1), Visual Studio and Xcode. The 3.18 floor comes from the\r\n11-vendored mimalloc, which is the default allocator; on an older CMake,\r\n12-configure with ``-DSTP_ALLOCATOR=system`` to skip it and use the C\r\n13-library's malloc instead.\r\n14-\r\n15:Dependencies\r\n16-------------\r\n17-\r\n18-STP relies on flex, bison and python3, plus at least one SAT backend.\r\n19-Nothing else has to be installed: with ``-DENABLE_AUTO_DOWNLOAD=ON`` the\r\n--\r\n31-.. code-block:: bash\r\n32-\r\n33:    sudo apt-get install git build-essential cmake bison flex python3\r\n34-\r\n35-A python3 interpreter is needed at build time -- it generates the AST kind\r\n36-tables -- and also for the Python interface and the test suite. git is needed\r\n37-to fetch the dependencies, which are cloned rather than downloaded as\r\n--\r\n40-The SAT backends bring their own dependencies, which are needed only if you\r\n41-build that backend, and which the ``scripts/deps`` script for each one names:\r\n42:CryptoMiniSat needs GMP (``libgmp-dev``), MiniSat needs zlib\r\n43-(``zlib1g-dev``). Neither is used by STP itself.\r\n44-\r\n45-STP has no submodules. Everything it does not contain itself is fetched\r\n46-at a pinned revision, and with ``-DENABLE_AUTO_DOWNLOAD=ON`` that needs\r\n--\r\n175-    git checkout 0a71f0c46903351543bf2f15ddb0df372b8471d6\r\n176-    mkdir build && cd build\r\n177:    cmake .. -DNOCADICAL=ON -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF -DSTATIC_BINARY=OFF \\\r\n178-             -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON\r\n179:    cmake --build . -j$(nproc)\r\n180:    sudo cmake --install .\r\n181-    command -v ldconfig && sudo ldconfig\r\n182-\r\n183:The commit to check out is the one ``cmake/FindCryptoMiniSat.cmake`` pins,\r\n184-and the flags are among those it builds that commit with. ``-DNOCADICAL=ON``\r\n185-is the one that matters (see below); the others make a static,\r\n186-position-independent library, which links into a shared ``libstp`` and a\r\n187-static one alike. Moving the pin in that file is what moves it for the\r\n--\r\n278-    cd minisat\r\n279-    mkdir build && cd build\r\n280:    cmake ..\r\n281:    cmake --build . -j$(nproc)\r\n282:    sudo cmake --install .\r\n283-    command -v ldconfig && sudo ldconfig\r\n284-\r\n285-The MiniSat STP builds, a commit on the ``ipasir-up`` branch of\r\n286-`stp/minisat <https://github.com/stp/minisat>`__, hosts the theory\r\n--\r\n312-   ``minisat/core/Solver.h`` and to the ``minisat`` libraries\r\n313--  ``-Dcryptominisat5_DIR:PATH=<path>`` -- the path to\r\n314:   ``cryptominisat5Config.cmake``\r\n315-\r\n316-If the development libraries were not installed, ``MINISAT_LIBDIR`` can\r\n317-be set to minisat's ``build`` directory, and ``cryptominisat5_DIR`` to\r\n318-CryptoMiniSat's.\r\n--\r\n326-be used instead, via ``-DSYMFPU_INCLUDE_DIRS=<directory containing the\r\n327-clone>`` -- that one is taken as-is, so it must already carry those\r\n328:fixes, which are in ``cmake/deps-utils/symfpu``.\r\n329-\r\n330-STP solves the SMT-LIB floating-point theory and exposes floating-point\r\n331-terms through the C, C++ (``stp/fp.hpp``) and Python APIs. Real literals\r\n332-under ``to_fp`` -- ``((_ to_fp 8 24) RNE 0.1)`` -- are folded to their\r\n--\r\n411-   otherwise ``ENABLE_AUTO_DOWNLOAD`` builds release 1.12.0\r\n412--  ``ENABLE_HIGHS_CUT_LOG`` -- with ``ENABLE_HIGHS``, build HiGHS with\r\n413:   ``cmake/deps-utils/highs-root-cut-log.patch``, which has it report how\r\n414-   it derived the cuts it adds at the root of a MIP search, so that\r\n415-   ``--lra-highs-cuts`` can rebuild them exactly. Off by default. An\r\n416-   installed HiGHS has to have been built with that patch\r\n417--  ``HIGHS_DIR`` -- the prefix of an installed HiGHS to use, rather than\r\n--\r\n477-\r\n478-T"]
[83.525092, "o", "here are three ways to set them, in decreasing order of friendliness:\r\n479:run ``cmake-gui`` on the source root instead of ``cmake``, which also\r\n480:lets you pick the generator; run ``ccmake``, which is the same idea in an\r\n481:ncurses terminal interface; or pass ``-D<VARIABLE>=<VALUE>`` to ``cmake``,\r\n482-which is best kept for scripts. An already-configured build can be\r\n483-changed with ``make edit_cache``, which reconfigures and regenerates.\r\n484-\r\n485-Link-time and profile-guided optimisation\r\n--\r\n641-\r\n642-    export STP_DEP_DIR=~/.cache/stp/deps          # configure.sh honours this\r\n643:    cmake -S . -B warm -G Ninja \\\r\n644-      -DSTP_DEP_DIR=$STP_DEP_DIR \\\r\n645-      -DFETCHCONTENT_BASE_DIR=~/.cache/stp/fetch \\\r\n646-      -DENABLE_AUTO_DOWNLOAD=ON\r\n647:    cmake --build warm --target deps\r\n648-\r\n649-then in every worktree:\r\n650-\r\n651-.. code-block:: bash\r\n---minisat files---\r\n/.\r\n/usr\r\n/usr/bin\r\n/usr/bin/minisat\r\n/usr/include\r\n/usr/include/minisat\r\n/usr/include/minisat/core\r\n/usr/include/minisat/core/Dimacs.h\r\n/usr/include/minisat/core/Solver.h\r\n/usr/include/minisat/core/SolverTypes.h\r\n/usr/include/minisat/mtl\r\n/usr/include/minisat/mtl/Alg.h\r\n/usr/include/minisat/mtl/Alloc.h\r\n/usr/include/minisat/mtl/Heap.h\r\n/usr/include/minisat/mtl/IntTypes.h\r\n/usr/include/minisat/mtl/Map.h\r\n/usr/include/minisat/mtl/Queue.h\r\n/usr/include/minisat/mtl/Sort.h\r\n/usr/include/minisat/mtl/Vec.h\r\n/usr/include/minisat/mtl/XAlloc.h\r\n/usr/include/minisat/simp\r\n/usr/include/minisat/simp/SimpSolver.h\r\n/usr/include/minisat/utils\r\n/usr/include/minisat/utils/Options.h\r\n/usr/include/minisat/utils/ParseUtils.h\r\n/usr/include/minisat/utils/System.h\r\n/usr/lib\r\n/usr/lib/libminisat.a\r\n/usr/lib/libminisat.so.2.1.0\r\n/usr/share\r\n/usr/share/doc\r\n/usr/share/doc/minisat\r\n/usr/share/doc/minisat/changelog.Debian.gz\r\n/usr/share/doc/minisat/copyright\r\n/usr/share/doc/minisat/minisat-user-guide.html\r\n/usr/share/doc-base\r\n/usr/share/doc-base/minisat.minisat-user-guide\r\n/usr/share/man\r\n/usr/share/man/man1\r\n/usr/share/man/man1/minisat.1.gz\r\n/usr/lib/libminisat.so\r\n/usr/lib/libminisat.so.2\r\n---cms files---\r\n/.\r\n/usr\r\n/usr/include\r\n/usr/include/cryptominisat5\r\n/usr/include/cryptominisat5/cryptominisat.h\r\n/usr/include/cryptominisat5/cryptominisat_c.h\r\n/usr/include/cryptominisat5/dimacsparser.h\r\n/usr/include/cryptominisat5/solvertypesmini.h\r\n/usr/include/cryptominisat5/streambuffer.h\r\n/usr/lib\r\n/usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu\r\n/usr/lib/cmake\r\n/usr/lib/cmake/cryptominisat5\r\n/usr/lib/cmake/cryptominisat5/cryptominisat5Config.cmake\r\n/usr/lib/cmake/cryptominisat5/cryptominisat5ConfigVersion.cmake\r\n/usr/lib/cmake/cryptominisat5/cryptominisat5Targets-relwithdebinfo.cmake\r\n/usr/lib/cmake/cryptominisat5/cryptominisat5Targets.cmake\r\n/usr/share\r\n/usr/share/doc\r\n/usr/share/doc/libcryptominisat5-dev\r\n/usr/share/doc/libcryptominisat5-dev/copyright\r\n/usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/libcryptominisat5.so\r\n/usr/share/doc/libcryptominisat5-dev/changelog.Debian.gz\r\n"]
